{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/apphost at exact clean pushed head a50973d11a2078495d80657a8e735dd3b3b8c8d5 on request/create-config-replacement-safety, answering 4f38749f. This is the implementation report for that request and it supersedes my earlier candidate at 3f431a32, which codex reviewed and returned as changes-requested.\n\nThe defect and the fix are unchanged from that review. CreateConfig created the configuration at its destination and, on a failed write or close, removed it again behind an os.SameFile guard, which read equal device and inode numbers as identity. Linux reuses a freed inode eagerly, so a configuration another process had stored at that path could answer as this call's file and be deleted. That is GitHub run 32670745698, and the defect is mine, from d4f54392. Creation now writes and closes a privately named staging file and hard-links it into place; every path removes only that staging name, so there is no identity to judge.\n\nWhat changed since 3f431a32. Only the architecture page, in the accompanying commit, plus the commit message trailers. codex approved Security and Simplification at 3f431a32 and requested changes on Architecture alone: the head changes the custody contract by requiring same-directory hard links and giving concurrent readers complete-only visibility, and AGENTS.md requires that contract change in the same exact head. It is now here, and a docs/reference/architecture.md artifact stands at this same head.\n\nGates. gofmt, git diff --check, go vet, GOOS=windows go build, go test -race over internal/apphost and internal/app, and go test ./... -count=1 across all thirty packages ran at 85e94539 and all exited zero with no failures and nothing cached. This head is that same tree: both commits carry tree f829aa83cc3a70b6dbedc3b715a70ab1fd1b841b, and the amend added only the second Rests-On trailer. I did not re-run the suite for the message change and I am not claiming that I did.\n\nTwelve mutations were measured against this tree, each confirmed applied by diff and confirmed to compile, with no survivors and no non-measurements. Deleting the os.ErrClosed guard on the fallback close, and storing a different but valid genesis, both survived the previous test file and are each now killed by exactly one new assertion.\n\nWhat this head still does not prove, unchanged from the last artifact and repeated so no reviewer has to hunt for it. TestCreateConfigLeavesAReplacementAtItsDestinationAlone passes against pre-fix code on APFS and pins the defect only where inode numbers are reused eagerly; its comment says so, and TestCreateConfigCleanupRemovesOnlyWhatItCreated is the platform-independent guard. The no-hard-link refusal is read from os.Link's single unbranched call site, not measured, because no such filesystem was mountable. Windows is compile-checked only. Nothing fsyncs before the link, so a crash can persist the directory entry ahead of the data. A staging file orphaned by a crash is never collected, matching WriteFileAtomically. If the link succeeds but the staging removal fails, the configuration is stored and CreateConfig still returns an error that AttachConfig treats as fatal, self-healing on retry.","body":{"commit":"a50973d11a2078495d80657a8e735dd3b3b8c8d5","path":"internal/apphost"}}